{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And as for those who are left among you, etc.</b> Meaning, those who remain after all this in their wickedness and did not return in repentance — in the same manner that He said above, ״וְאִם תֵּלְכוּ עִמִּי קֶרִי״ etc., so too He said, ״וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִים בָּכֶם״ — meaning, at the first measure, I will add, upon bringing upon them faintness, etc., <b>and they shall fall</b>, etc. <b>And as for those who are left</b>, etc. — meaning: those who did not return, etc. After all this they shall rot away, etc. And from the implication of the matter you know that even though destruction upon destruction may come upon them, the nation shall not be annihilated, as He says at the end: ״לֹא מְאַסְתִּים לְכַלּוֹתָם״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:29.040915119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}